Title: Mixer: channel list changes under the host audio lock; SDL2 device closed at mixer stop
Repository: boxer (https://github.com/alinebee/Boxer.git)
Date: 2026-10-02
Author: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Base-Commit: 0062fc18e154cde6cef3bf3329be4b0658597e31
Preceding-Patches:
  0001-aros-host-sdl-seam.patch
  0002-aros-config.patch
  0003-mount-colon-paths.patch
  0004-host-sdl3-core-audio-timer-on-sdl3-under-boxer-hos.patch
Problem: The host device callback (SDL2 audio thread, SDL3 device thread running the stream callback) walks mixer.channels and writes chan->done. MIXER_AddChannel and MIXER_DelChannel changed that list without the host lock, and MIXER_DelChannel freed the channel at once. Config::~Config deletes sections in reverse order, so every device (sblaster/OPL, gus, speaker, ...) removes its channel while the device callback still runs; the mixer section, registered earlier, stops last. A callback positioned on the removed channel then reads its next pointer and writes its done field after free. SDL2 also never closed the device in MIXER_Stop, so its callback kept running through the rest of the teardown until SDL_Quit (SDL3 already destroyed the stream there). Parameter changes (SetVolume/UpdateVolume/boxer_updateVolumes, SetFreq) only touch fields the callback does not read, and on AROS they run on the emulator task, so they were left unlocked; Enable and FillUp already locked.
Solution: MIXER_AddChannel links the fully initialised channel under MIXER_LockHost; MIXER_DelChannel unlinks and deletes under it. MIXER_Stop calls SDL_CloseAudio on the SDL2 host (joins the device thread); afterwards SDL_LockAudio/SDL_PauseAudio are no-ops, so later lock calls are safe. Both locks are recursive (SDL2 device mutex, SDL3 stream mutex) and are taken from inside MIXER_Mix handlers already, so a device that removes a channel from a handler does not deadlock; nothing waits for the callback while holding the lock (SDL_CloseAudio/SDL_DestroyAudioStream are called unlocked).
Platform-Scope: All non-Apple builds of the core, both hosts (BOXER_HOST=sdl2 and sdl3), AROS ABIv11 and mainline v1. The lock code compiles on any host.
Upstream-Status: local-only
Verification: 2026-10-02: a host race harness (not published; real mixer.cpp, pthread SDL stand-in, callback in a tight loop on its own thread, freed channels quarantined with next -> trap): before 2096/2065 freed-channel walks per 3 s (sdl2/sdl3) and 2.2 M SDL2 callbacks after MIXER_Stop; after 0 and 0, three runs each. Builds: build-core/build-ui sdl2 and sdl3 on ABIv11 and mainline v1. Guest runs on ABIv11.
Removal-Condition: When the core is replaced or its mixer is rewritten with its own list synchronisation.

diff --git a/DOSBox/src/hardware/mixer.cpp b/DOSBox/src/hardware/mixer.cpp
index f2ec9af7db04e512fed724b29bc019796912c7e7..17732bf9ee2ebac5efe2068091863152b96055d3 100644
--- a/DOSBox/src/hardware/mixer.cpp
+++ b/DOSBox/src/hardware/mixer.cpp
@@ -102,10 +102,15 @@ MixerChannel * MIXER_AddChannel(MIXER_Handler handler,Bitu freq,const char * nam
 	chan->handler=handler;
 	chan->name=name;
 	chan->SetFreq(freq);
-	chan->next=mixer.channels;
 	chan->SetVolume(1,1);
 	chan->enabled=false;
+	//--Modified 2026 for the AROS port: the device callback walks this list
+	//on its own thread; link the fully built channel under the host lock.
+	MIXER_LockHost();
+	chan->next=mixer.channels;
 	mixer.channels=chan;
+	MIXER_UnlockHost();
+	//--End of modifications
 	return chan;
 }
 
@@ -119,17 +124,26 @@ MixerChannel * MIXER_FindChannel(const char * name) {
 }
 
 void MIXER_DelChannel(MixerChannel* delchan) {
+	//--Modified 2026 for the AROS port: devices are destroyed before the
+	//mixer (Config::~Config runs sections in reverse), so channels are
+	//removed while the device callback may be walking the list and writing
+	//chan->done. Unlink and free under the host lock; the callback then
+	//either finished with the channel or never sees it. The lock is
+	//recursive on both hosts and the callback never waits on this thread.
+	MIXER_LockHost();
 	MixerChannel * chan=mixer.channels;
 	MixerChannel * * where=&mixer.channels;
 	while (chan) {
 		if (chan==delchan) {
 			*where=chan->next;
 			delete delchan;
-			return;
+			break;
 		}
 		where=&chan->next;
 		chan=chan->next;
 	}
+	MIXER_UnlockHost();
+	//--End of modifications
 }
 
 void MixerChannel::UpdateVolume(void) {
@@ -580,6 +594,12 @@ static void MIXER_Stop(Section* sec) {
 		mixer_stream=NULL;
 		SDL_DestroyAudioStream(stream);
 	}
+#else
+	//--Modified 2026: SDL2's device stayed open until SDL_Quit, so its
+	//callback kept running while the rest of the core was torn down.
+	//SDL_CloseAudio joins the device thread; afterwards SDL_LockAudio and
+	//SDL_PauseAudio are no-ops, so later MIXER_LockHost calls are safe.
+	if (!mixer.nosound) SDL_CloseAudio();
 #endif
 }
 
